            <title>[LU-20336] osd_grow_blocksize() often returns EOPNOTSUPP</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20336</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;During simple workloads (like kernel compilation), I often see:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    LustreError: 1711:0:(osd_io.c:1005:osd_grow_blocksize()) \&lt;br/&gt;
      object &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0x280000400:0xf2cf00:0x0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;: change block \&lt;br/&gt;
      size4096 -&amp;gt; 131072 error rc = -95&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;dnode_set_blksz() returns EOPNOTSUPP on Linux when it finds that blocks beyond the first block are allocated or dirty. This error appears to be benign, but noisy.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
